THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

The license above applies to the original Himalaya Non-stationary BEM code
authored by Durga Acharya. It does not replace the terms governing bundled
third-party software or data, which retain their own licenses and copyrights:

  * hmmvp0.16/ - HMMVP: Software to Compute Hierarchical-Matrix Matrix-Vector
    Products, version 0.16, by Andrew M. Bradley. Licensed under the Eclipse
    Public License 1.0 (http://www.opensource.org/licenses/eclipse-1.0).
    See hmmvp0.16/readme.txt.

  * tools/CalcTriDisps.m, tools/tridisloc3d.m - Triangular dislocation element
    routines, Copyright (c) 2006 Brendan Meade, released under the MIT license;
    the full notice is retained in each file header. tools/CalcTriDisps_O.m and
    tools/CalcTriStrains_O.m are modified versions of that code by Wen-Jeng
    Huang. These routines compute the stress kernel and the elastic Green's
    functions used by this software. The author asks that the code and the
    accompanying paper be cited as:

        Meade, B. J. (2007). Algorithms for the calculation of exact
        displacements, strains, and stresses for triangular dislocation elements
        in a uniform elastic half space. Computers & Geosciences, 33(8),
        1064-1075. doi:10.1016/j.cageo.2006.12.003

  * tools/Nikkhoo/, tools/TDstressHS.m - Triangular dislocation routines,
    Copyright (c) 2014 Mehdi Nikkhoo (Nikkhoo & Walter, 2015), released under the
    MIT license; the full notice is retained in each file header. Bundled as an
    optional alternative kernel; not used by the default code path.

  * build_mesh/make_mesh_elastic.m, build_mesh/make_mesh_visco.m,
    tools/make_tri_mesh.m - Triangular mesh generation based on code by
    Yo Fukushima (2010).

  * ne_10m_coastline/ - Natural Earth 1:10m Coastline shapefile, version 4.1.0.
    Natural Earth raster and vector map data is in the public domain
    (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/).

  * tools/cmap.mat - Bundled colormap data.

  * vel_field_lindsey/ - GPS velocity data from Lindsey et al. (2018).

  * build_mesh/him_contours_45.txt - Fault geometry derived from Slab2
    (Hayes et al., 2018) and Hubbard et al. (2016).

  * Green_function_visco/ - Green's functions computed with VISCO3D (Pollitz).

See the "Third-party software and data" section of README.md for details.
